    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d179-a4">

                <pb facs="0248" n="176" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg176"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Conger to the Prince of Ching.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States of America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Peking, China</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1904-07-06"><hi rendition="#italic">July 6,
                                1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Imperial Highness</hi>: I have the honor to
                    inform Your Imperial Highness that I am in receipt of a letter from Mr. A. W.
                    Bash, agent of the China Investment &amp; Construction Co., requesting me to
                    forward to Your Imperial Highness the inclosed letter, in which he makes
                    application for a concession to provide a loan for the construction of a railway
                    line from Chengtu, Szechuen, to Chungking and Hankow, in case the viceroy of
                    Szechuen should find himself unable to prosecute his reported plan to raise
                    money from native sources for such a line. He begs that your board will place
                    this application on file.</p>
                <p>I have much pleasure in complying with Mr. Bash’s request and so forward the
                    application inclosed.</p>
                <p>I avail myself of the opportunity to renew, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
